{"kind":"report","text":"Completed the full static preliminary R2 revision 6 assessment under request f89713612ed440e1505eb16d7cb5cb6a8eb00d3e and promise d461e612aa28bfb178cc945b74a77cfac68ba7d9, preserving the complete original fe47970e/8da8b218 commission and Hugh's d4e07064 direction. Exact assessed head: abc9c365a1f07cfbe88f3a444e4275cf8cf89bbd. This is a preliminary findings report on an unfiled design, not a guarded artifact verdict, adoption, implementation approval or runtime proof. R2 revision 7 e44fce7c and R3 revision 5 5ec08fab arrived during this assessment; their broad changes are not covered by this completed revision-6 reading.\n\nThe root reviewer read every byte of the main note (142719 bytes, 1849 newline-terminated lines), correction ledger (24501 bytes, 145 lines), and dated GitHub evidence (75661 bytes, 533 lines). Respective SHA-256 identities: 0eac90190303c2d212a49a2fa6ba4757d3decf6fe66a35faae64517d434b9af9; c444417cde951a6f58f76a9eb8a3221ffa0313e3994d5297435ea69f12397bee; b27421e4965c6b3b6fe6462e9c67e128a0531a79c286f1a21eb77f36ee139927. Parallel static readers independently checked the agreement/authorship, browser recovery and official-documentation sections. Root also read the relevant exact R1 revision-5 expected-revision and attribution rules, R3 revision-4 report/handover/staging rules, and current official GitHub review/closing/sub-issue documentation. No repository code, tests, builds, installations, provider probes or private diagnostic was executed.\n\nP1, high confidence — Negotiated terms can count as the planned terms without the parent's decision. Main lines 185,187 let propose-terms set conditions B and agree accept B while conditionsAt remains the original intent fact A. The report copies that fact (221). Completeness's written comparison (498–502) treats it as the child's original conditions fact and requires accepted-as-delivered only when that fact differs. Reachable design witness: required child created for A; performer proposes B; requester agrees; reports and independently accepts delivery of B; integrator selects that acceptance under the original plan. The fact comparison still matches A, without the parent's recorded decision accepting B instead. Keep the goal revision fact separate from the exact agreed terms. Compare the report's immutable accepted agreement/terms with the planned conditions; require canonical equality or a parent decision naming this acceptance. Validate both changed and equal negotiated terms. This is a semantic requirement beyond the already declared G10 operand gap. Design repair small; implementation risk medium.\n\nP1, high confidence — The manifest's authors omit the source commitment's inherited work. Main 393,475–477 derive authors from selected reports plus this new manifest act's attribution. They do not include the source commitment/hold named as preparation data. Witness: U reports commit C under accepted commitment K; reporting releases its hold but leaves K standing (R3 revision4:688). V takes over K after the hold ends (R2:192), takes a new hold, and receives C with its recorded authors (612–615). V integrates C and proposes a manifest with no selections, explicitly allowed by 479–481,526–530 and R3:897–901. The new act contributes V; the empty selection contributes nobody. U can pass the manifest's notIn[authors] review guard (396) despite its included contribution. R1:834–849 already retains U in K's attribution, but this path never takes it. Carry authenticated source-commitment attribution, including inherited inputs, through staging/pin evidence and union it into the manifest's authors independently of selected reports. Do not substitute arbitrary Git author text. Verify the handover/no-selection witness and its controller/principal cases. Design repair small; implementation risk medium.\n\nP2, high confidence — Any-key transition replacements need the same original expected revision to exclude one another. Main 1103 claims both cannot admit because each names an expected item revision. R1:689–696 checks each intent's own map. An original transition expecting r can admit, move the item to r+1 and lose its reply; another device can read r+1 and sign a corrected transition expecting r+1 with another key. Both admit. Explicitly require preserving the original expected map for the advertised exclusion, or disclose the possible second admission. Preserve the sound same-key idempotency rule in 1102. Verify a refreshed-revision witness separately from a shared-revision witness. Design repair small; risk low.\n\nTwo smaller corrections: main 409 permits cancel-merge in intended/committed, while 830 presents that admitted control in unknown too, with a destination refusal. Align the guard and the browser affordance; this is not evidence of unsafe publication. Also qualify evidence fact 5.12 and main 1453: GitHub excludes not only the PR author but the person who assigned Copilot to the related issue from approving its resulting PR (https://docs.github.com/en/pull-requests/how-tos/review-pull-requests/reviewing-proposed-changes-in-a-pull-request). Preserve Artroom's explicit ownerMayReview policy choice. The claim at 1823 that GitHub closes a parent regardless of unresolved concerns is not stated by the checked closing/sub-issue guides; label it as an inference or omit it.\n\nArchitecture: The separation of commitments, holds, immutable agreements, selected accepted reports, exact manifests and destination-owned publication remains valuable and coherent. The two P1 findings affect the core claims of derived completeness and independent review. Complete their fact and attribution paths before commissioning executable definitions. Keep R1/R3/R4 dependencies with their owners and review the newly announced changes separately.\n\nSecurity: Signed-only mutation is consistent with the deliberate R3 retarget; do not restore legacy bearer mutation merely for compatibility. Refusal versus terminal settlement, durable